# PulseTrader — config reference (SAFE to commit; contains NO real secrets).
#
# HOW THE CLI ACTUALLY READS CONFIG — read this before trying to "seed" a key:
#
#   * `pulse compose` reads its API key from OLLAMA_API_KEY through the resolver in
#     src/adapters/secrets.rs (r1.s1.w2 — src/cli/compose.rs no longer holds any
#     resolution logic of its own). It searches FOUR locations, in this order:
#         1. the process environment variable OLLAMA_API_KEY
#         2. $PULSE_CONFIG_DIR/.env  (the ADR-0014 overlay; wins over the defaults)
#         3. a gitignored `.env` in the working dir or the crate manifest dir
#         4. `.env` in the application data directory —
#            ~/Library/Application Support/PulseTrader/.env, beside pulse.db
#     Location 4 is what makes a Finder-launched app work: it has no shell, so
#     locations 1 and 3 are unreachable for it.
#
#     PERMISSIONS ARE ENFORCED, FAIL-CLOSED. A `.env` is used only if it is owned by
#     the running user AND has no group or world permission bits (0600, or stricter
#     such as 0400). A looser file is REFUSED with an error naming the failed check
#     — it is never read, and resolution does NOT quietly fall through to the next
#     location. If `pulse compose` starts refusing a `.env` that used to work:
#         chmod 0600 .env
#     Every `.env` is read IN-PROCESS only and is NEVER committed.
#
#     There is no `pulse setup-keys` for this key and none is being built; seeding a
#     credential from inside the app is not yet supported (see below for why the
#     Keychain path is separate).
#   * The composer's base URL + model are CONFIG-DRIVEN (slice-close FIX A,
#     ADR-0013): they load from `config/prices.toml`'s `[llm]` table
#     (`base_url` / `model`) via src/agent/config.rs. A missing table/field falls
#     back to the compiled-in defaults in src/adapters/llm/openai_compat.rs
#     (`OLLAMA_BASE_URL` / `OLLAMA_MODEL_ID`). Neither is an environment variable
#     — the binary never reads this file for the endpoint or the model. Edit
#     `config/prices.toml` to change them.
#   * `pulse llm-check` reads its key ONLY from the macOS *data-protection*
#     Keychain (account `glm_api_key`) via `keyring` (src/adapters/secrets.rs,
#     FR-1/NFR-5) — NOT from this file. `security add-generic-password` writes the
#     *login* keychain, which `keyring` cannot see. The supported key-seed path is
#     `pulse setup-keys` (VS-1.3.4), which writes the data-protection Keychain
#     entry under this binary's own code identity.
#
# Z.AI coding endpoint — OpenAI-compatible API, consumed through pulsehive-openai's
# OpenAICompatibleProvider (the sole `pulsehive` importer, src/adapters/llm/
# openai_compat.rs). The shipped default moved here from Ollama Cloud on
# 2026-08-29; that subscription is dropped.
#
# The variable is still named OLLAMA_API_KEY — RETAINED naming debt, tracked
# separately. Put your Z.AI key in it; the resolver chain reads this name first and
# nothing else was renamed with the default flip.
#
# The `compose` API key — the ONLY variable this file contributes. Set it here
# (gitignored `.env`) or in the environment. The endpoint and model are NOT env
# vars: they live in `config/prices.toml`'s `[llm]` table. Earlier revisions of
# this file carried OLLAMA_BASE_URL / OLLAMA_MODEL_ID as "reference mirrors" of
# the compiled-in defaults; nothing ever read them, and a mirror that can drift
# from the value it mirrors is worse than no mirror, so they are gone.
OLLAMA_API_KEY=your-z-ai-api-key-here
